      "math_academy_id": "e-14337",
      "problem": "Expand $(2x^n-1)(2x^n+1).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of square formula:\n\n$$\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2x^n$ and $b=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{n}-1)(2{x}^{n}+1) & = \\\\ {(2{x}^{n})}^{2}-(1)^{2} & = \\\\ {2}^{2}\\cdot ({x}^{n})^{2}-1 & = \\\\ 4{x}^{2n}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
